  "worked_solution": "First, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\operatorname{cot}\u2061x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{cot}\u2061x+2 & =-2\\operatorname{cot}\u2061x+22 \\\\ 5\\operatorname{cot}\u2061x & =20 \\\\ \\operatorname{cot}\u2061x & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that $\\operatorname{cot}\u2061x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}\u2061x}.$ Therefore, the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}\u2061x=\\frac{1}{4}.\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arctan}\u2061(\\frac{1}{4})=0.244\\,978\u22480.245\\,0\n$$\n\nSince $0.245\\,0$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=0.245\\,0.$\n\nTo generate more solutions, we add and subtract integer multiples of $\\pi .$ Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2}=-\\pi +x=-\\pi +0.245\\,0=-2.896\\,6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solutions are $x=0.245\\,0,-2.896\\,6.$\n\nFinally, the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$ is \n\n$$\n0.245\\,0\\cdot (-2.896\\,6)\u2248-0.7\n$$\n\nrounded to one decimal place.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
